s://www.meetup.com/humanist_canada/events/316526425/","description":"**Join us the 4th Friday of every month at 6 pm at Cherie Bistro for a get-together jointly hosted by the Humanist Association of Toronto and Toronto Oasis. Catch up with friends and welcome new people. Please RSVP on Meetup so that we can make reservations.**","startDate":"2026-10-23T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Cherie Bistro","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"538 Church St, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Humanist Association of Toronto (HAT) Meetup Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/humanist_canada/"},"performer":"Humanist Association of Toronto (HAT) Meetup Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Dopamin Nation Finding Balance in the Age of Indulgence\n/ book discussion","url":"https://www.meetup.com/auravista-movement/events/316757346/","description":"“Brilliant . . . riveting, scary, cogent, and cleverly argued.”—Beth Macy, author of Dopesick,\nas heard on Fresh Air\n\nThis book is about pleasure. It’s also about pain. Most important, it’s about how to find the delicate balance between the two, and why now more than ever finding balance is essential. We’re living in a time of unprecedented access to high-reward, high-dopamine stimuli: drugs, food, news, gambling, shopping, gaming, texting, sexting, Facebooking, Instagramming, YouTubing, tweeting . . . The increased numbers, variety, and potency is staggering. The smartphone is the modern-day hypodermic needle, delivering digital dopamine 24/7 for a wired generation. As such we’ve all become vulnerable to compulsive overconsumption.\n\nIn Dopamine Nation, Dr. Anna Lembke, psychiatrist and author, explores the exciting new scientific discoveries that explain why the relentless pursuit of pleasure leads to pain . . . and what to do about it. Condensing complex neuroscience into easy-to-understand metaphors, Lembke illustrates how finding contentment and connectedness means keeping dopamine in check. The lived experiences of her patients are the gripping fabric of her narrative. Their riveting stories of suffering and redemption give us all hope for managing our consumption and transforming our lives. In essence, Dopamine Nation shows that the secret to finding balance is combining the science of desire with the wisdom of recovery.","startDate":"2026-10-23T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Conference room","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Maple","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"100 Eagle Rock Way L6A 5B9,, Maple, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"AuraVista Movement","url":"https://www.meetup.com/auravista-movement/"},"performer":"AuraVista Movement"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Friday Dink & Strategy Clinic (1hr Lesson + Optional 1hr Game)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/playtogether/events/316784344/","description":"### **Friday Dink & Strategy Clinic (1hr Lesson + Optional 1hr Game)**\n\n* **6:00 PM - 7:00 PM:** Pickleball Dink & Strategy Clinic (GTA Pickleball Lessons)\n* **7:00 PM - 8:00 PM (Optional):** Extra hour of game play available for an extra $5 per person. (Note: The optional extra hour (7-8 PM) requires at least 4 players to agree and depends on court availability. Please let me know early if you are interested!)\n\n**Are you ready to elevate your pickleball game?** Join our exclusive, small-group clinic designed for players who want to move beyond just hitting hard and master the soft game. If you want to improve your dinking, court positioning, and stacking strategies, this session is perfect for you!\n\n**Meet Your Instructor** Hi, I'm Jeong, an NCCP-certified Level 2 pickleball and tennis instructor based in the GTA. I focus on helping players build solid technical fundamentals and strategic court awareness to win more rallies.\n\n**Verified Coach Profiles & Reviews**\n\n* [Superprof.ca](https://www.superprof.ca/nccp-certified-tennis-pickleball-instructor-teaching-the-basic-theory-and-practical-skills-tennis-pickl.html)\n* [Teachme.to](https://teachme.to/listings/pickleball/pickleball-with-jeong-sohn?skill=pickleball&latitude=43.866955&longitude=-79.440567)\n* [Playtogether.ca](https://playtogether.ca/about/)\n\n**What to Expect (60-Minute Session):**\n\n* **Warm-up & Assessment:** Quick rallies to assess your current level and identify key areas for improvement.\n* **Core Skills Training:** Step-by-step drills focusing on dink consistency, tactical positioning, and an introduction to stacking strategies.\n* **Guided Match Play:** Apply what you've learned in organized mini-games with real-time, personalized feedback.\n\n**Event Details:**\n\n* **Location:** Swing Star (5 Connie Crescent Unit 1, Vaughan, ON)\n* **Date & Time:** Every (Fri) 6-7pm\n* **Skill Level:** Beginner to Low-Intermediate\n* **Spots Available:** Strictly limited to 6-8 players to ensure quality coaching.\n* **Fee:** $20 (Covers court usage, practice balls, and instruction).\n* **Min-Max** Students: 3-6 (If there are fewer than 3 registrations, the amount paid via PayPal will be refunded via e-Transfer)\n* **Optional Extra Hour**: If you'd like to stay and play games after the 6-7 PM lesson, an additional hour (7-8 PM) is available for just **$5 per person**. This option is available if at least 4 players stay!","startDate":"2026-10-23T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Swing Star - Indoor Golf And Pickleball","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Vaughan","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1-15 Connie Crescent,, Vaughan, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Play Together Pickleball GTA for all levels","url":"https://www.meetup.com/playtogether/"},"performer":"Play Together Pickleball GTA for all levels"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Mississauga- let’s speak French/ Parlons français","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/events/314155007/","description":"Let’s get together to speak French! We’ll enjoy tea/coffee and some icebreaker games. Everyone is welcome.\n\nVenez parler français!\n\nÀ bientôt,\n\nHassane.\n\n\\*Merci beaucoup de vous être inscrit(e) à notre prochaine rencontre! Nous sommes ravis de votre présence.\nAfin de permettre à d’autres de se joindre à nous, nous vous demandons respectueusement :\n\n1. **Si vos plans changent,** veuillez mettre à jour votre statut (passer à 'Non') le plus rapidement possible pour libérer votre place.\n2. **Si vous êtes sur la liste d'attente,** merci de ne pas vous présenter à l'événement. Votre statut doit être confirmé pour pouvoir participer. Veuillez vous inscrire directement aux prochaines dates disponibles.\n\nAu plaisir de vous accueillir!\n\n\\*To allow others to join us, we respectfully ask that you:\n\n* **If your plans change,** please update your RSVP status (change it to 'No') as quickly as possible to free up your spot.\n* **If you are on the waiting list,** please do not show up for the event. Your status must be confirmed to participate. Instead, please register directly for the next available dates.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nVeuillez noter que pour profiter pleinement de nos échanges, une aptitude de base à la conversation est vivement souhaitée : ce groupe est un cercle de discussion convivial et non un cours de langue.\n\nPlease note that to fully enjoy the experience, a basic speaking aptitude is recommended: this group is a social conversation circle, not a formal teaching class.\n\nWe look forward to welcoming you!\n\nPlease join our WhatsApp group:\n\nhttps://chat.whatsapp.com/LRUdXbjpG8I9aph4dU6Go8","startDate":"2026-10-23T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Chocolate and love cafe","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"5985 Rodeo Dr Unit 14, Mississauga, ON L5R 3V6,, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/"},"performer":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Casual Board Games and Pub Social After","url":"https://www.meetup.com/boardgamestoronto/events/316788387/","description":"The Board Games event is a fun, sociable and charitable event\n\nWe are a fun, friendly and kind group of people mostly in our 20s, 30s and 40s. Beginners are welcome! We are a very inclusive and social group and we teach people how to play games they have not played before :)\n\nWe provide a variety of 40+ board games. The games usually take 5 or 10 minutes to learn and 30 to 60 minutes to play.\n\nPlay in French: On the last Friday of the month, we're offering a table where the games are played in French. Anyone with an intermediate level of French who wants to practice while playing is welcome to join. Just ask for Philippe when you arrive.\n\n**Time**\n\n*Board Games Start time: 630pm\n- Board Games end time: 10pm\n*Eat / Drink/ Socialise at a nearby pub afterwards\n\n**Location**\n\n30 Leeds St, Toronto, ON M6G 3R8 (Ukrainian Catholic Church of the Holy Protection)\n\nThe entrance to the board game room is at the back of the Church. There is a sign on the door that says BOARD GAMES GROUP.\n\nPlease use the map provided on the event page also.\n\nPayment\n**There are two ways to pay**\n**10 by Cash - coins are not accepted. Only bills.****\n**11.55 by Debit/Credit card\n\n**Charity Donations**\n\n- This is a not-for-profit initiative. Revenue go towards covering costs of the event including venue, insurance marketing, refreshments and board games. Any surplus revenue is donated to charity\n\n**Food and drink**\n\n*Everyone will get cookies/candy for free\n- Cups will be provided for tap water\n*Bring your own food and drink.\n- Please do not bring CHIPS AND CRACKERS as they make a mess and are greasy\n***ALCOHOL IS PROHIBITED AND WE HAVE A ZERO TOLERANCE POLICY ON THIS - there are no second chances**\n\nPhotos will be taken at the event and posted publicly for marketing purposes. Please only attend if you are ok with this or tell me when you arrive that you do not want to be in any photos\n\nThe event is officially hosted by Ace of Math Learning Program Ontario Inc.","startDate":"2026-10-23T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Ukrainian Catholic Church of the Holy Protection","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"30 Leeds St, Toronto, ON M6G 3R8, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Board Games and Social","url":"https://www.meetup.com/boardgamestoronto/"},"performer":"Board Games and Social"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Free Friday night movie @ Innis Town Hall. Deliverance","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316743864/","description":"🏕️ Free Movie Night: Deliverance — A Classic That Will Make You Think Twice About Camping!\n\nLooking for something a little darker this Halloween season? Join us Friday, October 23 at Innis Town Hall for a FREE screening of the 1972 survival thriller Deliverance. 🎬\n\n📍 Innis Town Hall\n2 Sussex Avenue, Toronto\n🎬 Movie starts: 7:10 PM\n⏱️ Runtime: 109 minutes\n\n🌲 About the Movie\n\nFour friends head into the wilderness for a canoe trip down a remote river before a proposed dam changes the landscape forever.\n\nWhat begins as an adventurous weekend quickly becomes a fight for survival as they encounter increasingly dangerous circumstances deep in the backcountry.\n\nStarring Jon Voight, Burt Reynolds, Ned Beatty and Ronny Cox, Deliverance is one of the most famous—and unsettling—survival movies ever made.\n\n🎥 Watch the trailer on YouTube:\n\"Watch the Deliverance (1972) Trailer\" ([https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Deliverance+1972+official+trailer](https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Deliverance+1972+official+trailer))\n\n👋 Meet Nick\n\nMeet Nick in the lobby before the movie.\nI'll have a Meetup sign so you can easily find me.\n\n💰 FREE EVENT!\n\nThere are NO charges or fees for this Meetup.\n\nPlease respect your RSVP—if you RSVP, please make every effort to attend.\n\nNot sure about your schedule yet? That's okay! You can simply just show up if you're unsure whether you'll be able to make it. No pressure to RSVP.\n\nCome out, meet some fellow movie fans, and experience one of the most iconic—and unforgettable—films of the 1970s. 🏕️🎬\n\nJust remember: this is probably not the movie to watch right before planning your next canoe trip. 😬","startDate":"2026-10-23T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Innis Town Hall","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"University of Toronto - St. George Campus, 2 Sussex Avenue, Toronto, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"SOMA - Conscious Connected Breathwork ($50-70)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soma-breathwork-embodied-practice-toronto/events/316735654/","description":"**Use the wisdom of your breath to reconnect with your body, emotions, and present moment.**\nExperience Conscious Connected Breathwork in a safe and nourishing environment.\n\n**A Small Group Experience**\nTo keep the experience intimate and allow for individual attention and support, each SOMA session is limited to **12 participants**.\n\n**Flexible Pricing**\nChoose the rate that feels right for you:\n**$50 - Accessible**\nFor those who would appreciate a lower-cost option.\n**$60 - Standard**\nThe regular rate that helps sustain SOMA.\n**$70 - Supporter**\nFor those who are able to contribute a little more toward making SOMA accessible to others.\nAll three rates include the same SOMA experience.\n\n**Registration**\nRegistration and payment are completed through Eventbrite, which is the official registration system for this session.\n[https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/soma-conscious-connected-breathwork-session-tickets-1999809548192](https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/soma-conscious-connected-breathwork-session-tickets-1999809548192)\n**Please note:** Meetup RSVP does not constitute registration or reserve a spot for the session.\n\n**What to Expect**\nYou will be guided through a conscious breathing technique that supports a shift from mental activity into a more present and embodied experience. The practice may bring emotional release, surface underlying thoughts or patterns, and deepen your connection with yourself and others.\n**The experience includes:**\n\n* Arrive & settle in\n* Instructions, safety guidelines, and setting of intention\n* Active breathwork journey\n* Integration - circle sharing (optional)\n\nThe session is designed for both beginners and experienced practitioners.\n\n**What to Bring**\n\n* Comfortable clothes\n* Yoga mat\n* Blanket - blankets will be provided, but you may prefer to bring your own\n* Eye mask (optional)\n* Water bottle\n\n**Safety**\nConscious Connected Breathwork is an active somatic practice that may bring up strong physical or emotional sensations, including emotional release, dizziness, tingling, or temporary discomfort. Participation is voluntary and you are responsible for your own wellbeing throughout the session. You may pause or stop at any time.\nThis practice is not recommended for individuals who are pregnant or who have serious cardiovascular, neurological, or psychiatric conditions. If you are unsure, please consult a medical professional before attending.\nUpon registration, you will receive a waiver to complete prior to the session.\n\n**About the Facilitator**\nKonstantin’s path into breathwork began through his own process of reconnecting with emotional presence and the body. A retreat in Mexico first introduced him to the power of conscious breathing as a tool for inner exploration and regulation.\nSince then, he has integrated breathwork into his personal practice and facilitation work. He has been holding sharing circles and retreats for the past few years, creating spaces for emotional expression, presence, and connection.\nHe is a certified Conscious Connected Breathwork facilitator.","startDate":"2026-10-23T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https:/